WEBVTT

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.319
A Big Board map can give everyone in a room the same view of

00:00:03.319 --> 00:00:05.699
calls, stations, and resources.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.550
This training board starts with several kinds of pins and labels.

00:00:09.989 --> 00:00:13.189
A search and rescue team might use it to watch a staging area.

00:00:13.619 --> 00:00:17.600
An industrial response team could focus the same widget on its facility.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.689
Open Settings and choose Map.

00:00:20.379 --> 00:00:25.529
Under Map Options, Zoom Out to Show All Pins fits the view to the displayed pins.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:29.140
The Visible Pins switches control what the widget includes.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.530
Calls and linked calls have separate switches, so check both when choosing

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.819
what the board needs to show.

00:00:34.999 --> 00:00:39.490
Turn off Show Calls and leave stations, units, and personnel enabled.

00:00:39.909 --> 00:00:41.729
Save, then return to the map.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.270
The training call pins are gone while the other references remain.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.550
This is a display preference for the widget.

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:50.850
It does not close any calls or remove assignments.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.410
For a board that should stay centered on the same area, turn

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.769
off Zoom Out to Show All Pins.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.590
Enter a zoom and set the center with latitude and longitude.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.640
We use a Chicago center.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.310
Keep the minus sign in the west longitude.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.320
Turn on Hide Labels to simplify the view.

00:01:08.539 --> 00:01:12.099
After saving, check that the frame covers the area you intended.

00:01:12.499 --> 00:01:15.230
Our first zoom is too tight to show the resources.

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:19.389
Reopen Map settings and set the zoom to twelve, then save again.

00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:22.450
The wider view keeps the fixed center while bringing the

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.190
training pins back into the frame.

00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:27.519
Now the pins remain but their Resgrid names are hidden.

00:01:27.959 --> 00:01:30.329
Street names from the basemap are still visible.

00:01:30.829 --> 00:01:34.469
Some training pins share a location, so their icons overlap.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:38.969
A community paramedicine team could use fixed framing for an outreach area,

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:43.010
while a security team could keep the view centered on the sites it monitors.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:47.119
Check the actual board from its viewing distance after making changes.
